/* ==========================================================================
 * MY_UNIVERSITIES -- education provider directory dataset
 * --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * 391 institutions registered with **Education Malaysia Global Services
 * (EMGS)**, the body every international student pass for Malaysia is applied
 * for through. Generated by _tooling/build_dataset_my.py -- do not hand-edit.
 *
 * SOURCES
 *   EMGS institution register, 397 institutions, captured 2026-09-02.
 *     https://educationmalaysia.gov.my/api/college/index
 *   Malaysian Qualifications Register (MQR), Malaysian Qualifications Agency
 *     -- 20386 accredited programmes, captured 2026-09-02.
 *     https://www2.mqa.gov.my/mqr/
 *   QS World University Rankings 2027, published 18 June 2026 -- 32 Malaysian
 *     institutions, 31 of which are on this register.
 *
 * WHY EVERY INSTITUTION HERE CAN ENROL YOU
 *
 * EMGS is the single gateway: the institution lodges the application, EMGS
 * issues the Visa Approval Letter, and Immigration issues the Student Pass
 * against it. An institution not registered with EMGS has no route to apply,
 * so it cannot enrol an international student. Registration IS the permission
 * -- the same relationship CRICOS has in Australia -- so the cards' hardcoded
 * "Intl. Admits: Yes" is exactly true and not an inference.
 *
 * WHAT IS EXCLUDED, AND WHY
 *   6 rows on the register are not a place a student can study in Malaysia:
 *   two foreign ministries and a foundation that sponsor students rather than
 *   teach them, two campuses located outside Malaysia (London and Malta), and
 *   one row that is a person's name. Nothing is excluded on a judgement about
 *   quality. The list is asserted in the builder so a register update cannot
 *   silently change it.
 *
 * FIELDS
 *
 *   accredited  the institution's number of MQA-accredited programmes on the
 *               MQR -- a real published count off the regulator's own register,
 *               in the slot the UK page fills with an invented `offerRate`.
 *               It is NOT a selectivity figure, and the UI labels it
 *               "MQA accredited" for that reason. 283 institutions carry a
 *               count; 108 show "n/a" because they could not be resolved to
 *               the MQR under any name they are registered with. "n/a" is used
 *               rather than "0" deliberately: the MQR lists fully accredited
 *               programmes only, so an absence is not evidence of none.
 *   programs    the three commonest fields of study across those accredited
 *               programmes, using MQA's own NEC (National Education Code)
 *               broad-field classification. Empty where unmatched -- never
 *               guessed.
 *   type        "Research University" for the five MOHE-designated research
 *               universities (UM, USM, UKM, UPM, UTM); "Public University" for
 *               the other fifteen and for UiTM's branch campuses; then the
 *               register's own categories.
 *   location    town and state. The state is derived from the postcode in the
 *               address EMGS publishes, because Pos Malaysia allocates
 *               postcodes by state and the register's own state tag is wrong on
 *               a large minority of rows -- it files USM, in Gelugor, under
 *               Kuala Lumpur.
 *   rank        position in this directory. `ranked` is true only for the
 *               institutions QS 2027 actually covers; the rest render a dash.
 *               QS ranks Universiti Kuala Lumpur as one university but EMGS
 *               registers only its six institutes, so no row is given that
 *               position.
 *   alt         searched, never rendered: acronyms, the Malay/English twin of
 *               the name, and the state.
 *
 * NOTHING here is an invented per-institution statistic.
 * ========================================================================== */
